<title>MEXICO: Mexico says receives 5 bids for electricity plant.</title>
<headline>Mexico says receives 5 bids for electricity plant.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-07-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's state-owned Federal Electricity Commmission (CFE) said in a statement on Sunday that it had received technical offers from five consortiums to construct the thermo-electrical generating plant, Cerro Prieto IV.</p>
<p>It said the plant, just south of the city of Mexicali in Baja California, will be able to generate 100 megwatts.</p>
<p>It said the offers came from Marubeni Corp, Mitsubishi Corp, Kanematsu-ICA Fluor Daniel, Ansaldo de Mexico, and Ormet International-GEC Alsthom-Turalmex.</p>
<p>It said that the decision will be made by August 10.</p>
<p>((-- Robert Kozak, Mexico City newsroom +525 728 9559))</p>
</text>
